@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Local Aurora sunlight extension
+
+`0.1-aurora-shadow.1` extends the local water.3 contract. It is not an upstream
+Horizon API. Existing API lines retain their shaders, layouts and allocation behaviour.
+The extension requires a post stage, because it retains water.3 fog ownership.
+
+Only the material stage receives `sun_visibility(camera_relative_position, geometric_world_normal)`.
+Its result is 0..1, with 1 meaning sunlight is unoccluded. The pack decides how to
+combine it with sky light, block light, weather and status effects. A zero contrast
+option in the pack does not disable the engine's depth-map work.
+
+Material group 2 is engine-owned for this extension:
+
+| Binding | Resource |
+| --- | --- |
+| 0 | `texture_depth_2d` sunlight map |
+| 1 | comparison sampler, LessEqual, linear filtering |
+| 2 | 80-byte uniform: camera-relative matrix, texel size, fade start/end, enabled |
+
+Group 3 remains the water.3 frame and pre-translucent snapshot. Frame's memory
+layout is unchanged from water.3. Sky and post stages cannot sample the shadow map.
+The caster pass binds a separate group 2 holding only the matrix; it never binds
+the depth texture as input while writing it.
+
+The depth target is 2048² Depth32Float (16 MiB), standard 0..1 depth, cleared to 1.
+One orthographic projection spans 96 blocks across. Its x/y origin snaps to texels
+in double precision; the camera-relative matrix converts to f32 afterward.
+The light uses the same solar direction as the native shader Frame. Receivers fade
+between 32 and 44 blocks from the camera and at map borders. Casters are limited to
+96 blocks horizontally and to the light frustum; no guarantee for distant tall casters.
+Night, title screen, Nether and End disable reception and skip caster draws.
+The target is still cleared to avoid stale data. The pack fades reception near sunset.
+
+Caster selection uses the existing light-frustum section list, bypassing player
+frustum/occlusion. Direct instanced draws work with both main-terrain draw paths.
+Only solid/cutout terrain is drawn, with the same texture alpha threshold and opaque-leaf
+flag as the normal material pipeline. No entity, transparent, LOD or coloured shadows.
+Nine comparison samples soften edges; this is fixed PCF, not contact-hardening shadows.
+Depth/slope and receiver bias reduce acne but require live tuning for detached contacts.
+
+Tests cover projection direction, texel stability, WGSL translation, real material
+composition, and an actual GPU caster→receiver check using an opaque/transparent
+texture. The GPU test explicitly reports a skip without an adapter; setting
+`AURORA_REQUIRE_GPU=1` makes that condition fail, as the Aurora preview launcher does.
+Final visual quality and performance must be checked in the running game.
-- 
